      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`TraceReqContext.trace_slice_end` discards a slice without ending its span when\nthe slice name or level does not match the top of the stack, so that span is\nnever exported.\n\nOn `main` (`dd83b54611897a5f80f4df59e69756bd2fb4b8ab`),\n`python/sglang/srt/observability/trace.py` L665-672:\n\n```python\n        # check if slice_name matching and level matching\n        # unlikely path, excepting error API usage\n        if cur_slice.slice_name != name or cur_slice.level != level:\n            logger.warning(\n                f\"Slice name mismatch: {name} != {cur_slice.slice_name} or level mismatch: {level} != {cur_slice.level}\"\n            )\n            self.thread_context.cur_slice_stack.pop()\n            return\n```\n\nThe slice is popped, but `cur_slice.span` is never ended. After the pop nothing\nholds a reference to that span, so it stays recording for the life of the\nprocess and the span processor never sees it. The matching path ends the span\nat L692 before popping at L694, and `abort()` at L797-800 ends every slice span\nit discards:\n\n```python\n        while len(self.thread_context.cur_slice_stack) > 0:\n            if self.thread_context.cur_slice_stack[-1].span:\n                self.thread_context.cur_slice_stack[-1].span.end(end_time=ts)\n            self.thread_context.cur_slice_stack.pop()\n```\n\nSo this branch is the only place in the file that drops a slice span without\nending it.\n\nThe parent span is still ended by `abort()`/`trace_req_finish`, which is why\nthis shows up as a silently missing child span rather than a broken trace: the\nrequest trace is exported with one slice absent, and the `SLICE_START` timing\nfor that slice is lost.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`trace.py`: end the span before popping in the mismatch branch, guarded by\n`if cur_slice.span:` to match the existing style in `abort()`.\n\n`test_trace.py`: two regression tests. The existing\n`test_trace_slice_end_name_mismatch` asserts only that the stack was popped,\nwhich is true both before and after this change, so it cannot see the leak. The\nnew tests assert the discarded span is no longer recording, and cover both\nhalves of the condition (name mismatch and level mismatch).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable — tracing only, no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. The added work is one `span.end()` on a branch the comment\nalready marks as an unlikely error path.\n\n## Verification\n\nAgainst the unmodified file at `dd83b5461189`, driving the real\n`TraceReqContext` with an SDK tracer provider:\n\n| case | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| matching name (normal path) | 1 span exported | 1 span exported |\n| mismatched name | **0 spans exported**, span still recording | 1 span exported, ended |\n| mismatched level | **0 spans exported**, span still recording | 1 span exported, ended |\n\nRunning the two new tests against the pristine file fails both with\n`the discarded slice's span must be ended, not left recording`; the\npre-existing `test_trace_slice_end_name_mismatch` and the normal-path test pass\nin both states, so the failure isolates the defect.\n\n`ruff format` reports both files already formatted, `ruff check\n--select=F401,F821,UP037` passes, and `isort --check-only` with the repo's\n`.isort.cfg` passes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to Write documentations.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results (not applicable).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35490744730](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35490744730)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35490744638](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35490744638)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35490744758](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35490744758)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
